{
  "summary": "This change only touches documentation. DEPLOYMENT.md now lists exactly the eight prerendered HTML files the build writes, including dist/systems/index.html and dist/engagements/index.html. It names the seven sitemap pages, mentions dist/images/ copied from public/, and leaves the Security headers section unchanged. The built dist/sitemap.xml contains all seven URLs, so the docs and the output agree.\n\nThe headless audits are clean on phone and desktop:\n- axe reports no violations.\n- Lighthouse scores 100 for accessibility and best practices, and 93 for performance.\n- There is no horizontal overflow and no console errors.\n- The primary flow (Home → Book a consultation → Contact errors → success) passed at both viewports, along with the Systems, Engagements, Services, Training, About and 404 screens.\n\nThe only UI gap the audits show is four class names in the rendered markup that no CSS rule matches. I can't confirm from the files provided whether these are intentional hooks or dead styling. Nothing here breaks the primary flow or the required states.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/pages/HomePage.tsx",
      "issue": "Three Home class names match no CSS rule (style audit 'unmatched'): `home-page`, `examples` and `why-text`. The spec requires the Why text column beside the photo to be vertically centered. If `why-text` was meant to carry that alignment or the 7-column span, it currently does nothing. The audit screenshots suggest a parent rule handles the layout, but the class is dead either way.",
      "fix": "Either give these classes the intended rules in global.css or remove them from the markup. For example, `.why-text { align-self:center }` if centering relies on it, and `.examples` for the pale section spacing. This keeps 'every class has CSS' true."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ArchitectureDiagram.tsx",
      "issue": "The dark variant applies class `arch-dark`, but no CSS rule targets it. The dark diagram colours (navy-raised boxes, #5FC4C4 group labels, teal strokes) are therefore probably set inline or via attributes, and the class is unused. That splits the styling source of truth from the token-driven CSS.",
      "fix": "Move the dark-variant fills, strokes and label colours into `.arch-dark …` rules using the tokens (`--color-navy-raised`, `--color-accent-light`, `--color-accent`). Alternatively, drop the unused class."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "dist/sitemap.xml",
      "issue": "The sitemap lists /systems and /engagements after /contact. That order differs from the header navigation and from the page order in DESIGN.md and DEPLOYMENT.md (Services, Systems, Training, Engagements, About, Contact). It is still valid, but readers comparing the files will find it inconsistent.",
      "fix": "Reorder public/sitemap.xml to match the documented page order."
    }
  ]
}
